1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,120
And now, to you, Scoutmaster.

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,120
Hey, you ever hear of Ken Hubbard?

3
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:11,180
Ken?

4
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:12,740
K-I-N?

5
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:13,180
Hubbard?

6
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,260
I'll bet you haven't.

7
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,840
Ken was once a household name.

8
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:19,960
Yeah, he was a cartoonist.

9
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,740
He had cartoon in newspapers.

10
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:24,460
But this is like in the 1920s, 1930s.

11
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:27,460
No, no, I really, I don't go back that far.

12
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:32,620
But I learned a little bit about Ken because I saw something that he said, and I thought it was great.

13
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,020
This is what he said.

14
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:39,260
Boys will be boys, and so will a lot of middle-aged men.

15
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:48,580
Now, all the women who are listening, they just said amen because they understand this.

16
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,540
They know this.

17
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,580
They've known it for a long time.

18
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:55,060
But some of the men who are listening,

19
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:57,540
Hey, guys, just come over here for a moment.

20
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:03,600
If you didn't get that, if you didn't understand that,

21
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,200
go talk to your wife, and she will explain it to you.

22
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:07,820
Okay?

23
